## 1. Linear Search

### Problem

Search for `30` in:

```java
int[] arr = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};
```

### Code

```java
package p1;

public class SearchArray {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};

        int search = 30;

        boolean found = false;

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

            if (arr[i] == search) {
                found = true;
            }
        }

        if (found) {
            System.out.println("Element is found");
        } else {
            System.out.println("Element not found");
        }
    }
}
```

### Output

```text
Element is found
```

### Important Concept

This is **Linear Search**.

```text
10 → ❌
20 → ❌
30 → ✅
```

We check elements one by one.

### Why `boolean found`?

Initially:

```java
boolean found = false;
```

When found:

```java
found = true;
```

After searching:

```java
if (found)
```

### Complexity

```text
Time  : O(n)
Space : O(1)
```

