# 2. Find Largest Element

### Problem

```java
int[] arr = {10, 25, 7, 40, 15};
```

### Code

```java
package p1;

public class LargestEle {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {10, 25, 7, 40, 15};

        int largest = arr[0];

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

            if (arr[i] > largest) {
                largest = arr[i];
            }
        }

        System.out.println("The Largest element = " + largest);
    }
}
```

### Output

```text
The Largest element = 40
```

### Dry Run

```text
largest = 10

25 > 10 → largest = 25
7 > 25  → No
40 > 25 → largest = 40
15 > 40 → No
```

### Important Pattern

```java
int largest = arr[0];

for (...) {
    if (arr[i] > largest) {
        largest = arr[i];
    }
}
```

### Complexity

```text
Time  : O(n)
Space : O(1)
```

