# 10. Second Largest Element

### Problem

Find the second-largest element without sorting.

```java
{10, 25, 7, 40, 15}
```

### Code

```java
package p1;

public class SecondLargest {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {10, 25, 7, 40, 15};

        int largest = arr[0];
        int secondLargest = largest;

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

            if (arr[i] > largest) {

                secondLargest = largest;
                largest = arr[i];
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Second Largest = " + secondLargest);
    }
}
```

### Output

```text
Second Largest = 25
```

### 🧠 Key Idea

When a new largest is found:

```text
Old largest → secondLargest
New value   → largest
```

Example:

```text
largest = 25
secondLargest = 10

Find 40

secondLargest = 25
largest = 40
```

### Important Order

Correct:

```java
secondLargest = largest;
largest = arr[i];
```

Not:

```java
largest = arr[i];
secondLargest = arr[i];
```

### ⚠️ Interview Note

This basic version is enough for our first practice, but later we'll make it interview-ready by handling:

* Duplicate values
* Negative numbers
* Arrays with fewer than 2 elements
* Distinct vs non-distinct second largest

### Complexity

```text
Time  : O(n)
Space : O(1)
```

